                <pb facs="0975" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stockton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-18T10:00:00+01:00">March 18, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—7:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>14. Department’s telegram No. 9, February 24, 5 p.m. Federal Council approved
                    supplemental article and reservation yesterday. President expected to ratify
                    within a few days. Austrian Government will be prepared to exchange
                    ratifications whenever I have received American instrument of ratification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
